---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { site } from '../../content';
const path = '/alternatives/marsello-alternative';
const title = 'Marsello alternatives for Shopify cart recovery';
const desc = 'Retained loyalty, POS and recovery boundaries: decide what to retain, repair or replace for Shopify cart recovery.';
const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "Can I replace recovery without moving points?",
    "answer": "Potentially. Keep one program ledger and require the receiving sender to demonstrate current benefit eligibility, purchase exits and purpose-specific channel permissions."
  },
  {
    "question": "Is a balance export enough for a program migration?",
    "answer": "No. Preserve transactions, rule versions, tier basis, issued codes and outstanding benefits, and reconcile cross-store acceptance before moving authority."
  },
  {
    "question": "Does removing a POS discount restore points?",
    "answer": "Marsello documents that removing the discount does not refund points. Check code availability and points state separately in the proposed acceptance exercise."
  },
  {
    "question": "What is the illustrative discount cost?",
    "answer": "At $518 revenue and 35% margin, an 18% discount reduces fixed-goods-cost contribution from $181.30 to $88.06, losing $93.24 before other costs and reward liabilities."
  }
];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="py-16 md:py-24 container">
    <a href="/alternatives" class="link text-sm font-bold">← All alternatives</a>
    <h1 class="hero-title mt-6">Marsello alternatives for Shopify cart recovery</h1>
    <p class="mt-6 max-w-3xl text-xl text-slate-700">Retained loyalty, POS and recovery boundaries.</p>
    <div class="prose-shopify mt-10">
      <h2>Keep a working loyalty program when only recovery needs repair</h2>
      <p>Marsello can be valuable when staff and customers rely on one loyalty experience across online and physical sales. Its <a class="link" href="https://help.marsello.com/how-do-i-connect-my-shopify-site-to-marsello-marsello-help-center">Shopify site guide</a> describes customer/purchase sync and enabling sites for loyalty and marketing. Audit enabled sites and the recovery workflow before replacing a working points program. Keeping the ledger and changing only messaging can preserve staff routines and earned benefits if the sender can consume authoritative eligibility without changing balances.</p>
      <h2>Choose retained program or full replacement</h2>
      <p>For a retained program, Marsello remains the points and reward authority; a separate recovery sender receives only the necessary customer, order and benefit state. Evaluate <a class="link" href="/alternatives/omnisend-alternative">a combined messaging workspace</a> or <a class="link" href="/alternatives/klaviyo-alternative">a broader retention workflow</a> for this receiving role. A full replacement is useful when a demonstrable program requirement cannot be repaired and the receiving ledger can preserve outstanding obligations. Neither link certifies ledger migration, POS support or a connector. Compare account-specific costs for enabled locations, program features, messaging and parallel operation against the value of preserving the existing program.</p>
      <h2>Name the source of every balance and benefit</h2>
      <p>Build a register of store/POS location, customer ID, order and refund IDs, points earned/spent/expired, manual adjustments, tier basis and effective dates, issued reward codes and redemption status. Assign a program owner to balances and a sending owner to messages. Preserve the ledger history and rule versions, not just a balance field or VIP tag. A shared email address is insufficient to merge household members. Define who may correct an adjustment, which system supplies current benefit eligibility and how a recipient sees the same promise online and at the till.</p>
      <h2>Proposed ledger and refund acceptance fixtures</h2>
      <p>These are proposed exercises, not tests performed here. Record a test purchase online, earn points under the configured rules, then partially refund it after a tier transition. Compare the source order, ledger delta, tier decision and sender eligibility; require an explanation for each difference. The <a class="link" href="https://help.marsello.com/how-do-i-automatically-remove-loyalty-points-for-shopify-orders-marsello-help-center">Shopify points guide</a> ties point removal to configured payment statuses and describes proportional removal when partially refunded status is selected. Document your actual settings rather than assuming every refund reverses every benefit. Deliver the same refund twice and an older paid event afterward: neither should create a second debit or restore a superseded entitlement.</p>
      <h2>Accept cross-store reward continuity</h2>
      <p>Issue a test reward online and attempt its use at an enabled POS location. The operator must reconcile the same customer, code, points debit and remaining liability in both views. Repeat after removing the reward from the sale. Marsello’s <a class="link" href="https://help.marsello.com/shopify-pos-common-questions-marsello-help-center">POS FAQ</a> says removing a discount does not refund points and that the code can remain available. Treat code availability, points balance and order payment as separate states. A replacement must demonstrate the intended behavior for claimed but unused codes, expired benefits, tier changes and inactive locations before any historical liability is written off. Loyalty membership alone does not grant email or SMS marketing permission.</p>
      <h2>Make recovery respect the program</h2>
      <p>For a mobile interruption, restore the cart without spending a reward again. For shipping shock, show the actual shipping benefit only if the member qualifies. Gift sizing requires guidance and a valid product, not a points promise. A minimum-order block must distinguish spend required for checkout from spend required for a reward. A financing interruption must not be recorded as a completed purchase earning points. An unavailable variant should not invite redemption for an unusable offer. A stacked coupon fixture must reconcile the recovery incentive with the claimed reward and stacking rules. Include repeat purchasers across online/POS to ensure loyalty status does not enroll an already completed order in recovery.</p>
      <h2>Own the queues and the rollback ledger</h2>
      <p>Preserve permission sources, timestamps, purposes, channel withdrawals and suppressions independently of membership. Map customer, store, checkout, order and event identifiers. Recheck purchase, cancellation, inventory and current permission before enrollment and send. Give each pending recovery, loyalty, welcome and SMS message one active owner; reconcile old queues before enabling replacements. Deduplicate replay by stable store/event/purpose/action keys. If reverting, pause new sends and ledger writers, reconcile delivered messages and actual points/code changes, then resume only eligible work from current state. Do not restore an old balance snapshot over valid transactions or send a second reward announcement for the same issuance.</p>
      <h2>Count reward cost as well as discount cost</h2>
      <p>Illustrative fixed-goods-cost example: $518 at 35% pre-discount margin gives goods cost $336.70 and contribution $181.30. An 18% recovery discount reduces revenue to $424.76 and contribution to $88.06, a loss of $93.24 before messaging, fees, shipping and returns. Add reward redemption cost and outstanding benefit liability separately without counting the same discount twice. Compare eligible member/nonmember and online/POS cohorts with a suitably sized holdout; attribution is not incrementality. Review actual order and ledger reconciliation when enough evidence exists. No universal migration duration or discount schedule establishes that replacement is profitable.</p>
      <p>Primary documentation checked November 25, 2026. Account settings and receiving-system acceptance still need merchant verification.</p>
    </div>
    <FaqSection faqs={faqs} title="FAQ: Marsello alternatives" />
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
